// EXPECTED: semantic error — "invalid assignment". `x > 0` evaluates to
// a bool, being assigned into `y`, declared as int. Kept deliberately
// distinct from type_mismatch.mini (numeric-into-bool) to test the
// opposite direction (bool-into-numeric), per the manual's "or similar"
// wording in Section 4.5.

int x;
int y;
x = 5;
y = (x > 0);
print y;
